 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 381 of the laws of 2012 amending the education law\nrelating to the licensure of private proprietary schools, in relation to the\neffectiveness of certain provisions of such chapter",
    "basePrintNo": "S8215",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8215-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §12, Chap 381 of 2012",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8215\n\nSPONSOR: LAVALLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 381 of the laws of 2012 amend-\ning the education law relating to the licensure of private proprietary\nschools, in relation to the effectiveness of certain provisions of such\nchapter\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nExtends certain provisions for licensure for private career schools.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Extends certain provisions relating to private career school\nlicenses for another three years.\n\nSection 2. Provides that this act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn 2012, vital work was done to update the law in relation to non-degree\nproprietary schools. This major overhaul was necessary to ensure that\nthere was a proper oversight for this area of institutions that have\ngrown since the law was last substantially amended in 1990. This legis-\nlation provides for an extension of three years\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
